```
ROLE: product_realist  VOTE: red
REAL_USE_CASE: Long-horizon RAG agents where ~53% of retrievals return content already resident in the live context window (CoQA 4,764 turns, M1=0.532). The narrow need would be a cheap pre-retrieval check that skips redundant fetches without harming task accuracy.
OPERATIONAL_SIGNIFICANCE: Microbenchmark-only. L0's +9 to +19pt precision edge over random evaporated on real data; in-context gate vs semantic query cache at matched ~29% skip shows real LLM token-F1 0.4505 vs 0.4501, delta +0.0004 with bootstrap 95% CI [-0.0045,+0.0053] = zero measurable difference. Precision Δ(gate-cache) CI straddles 0 for every deployment-relevant skip-rate ≥20%. The 'live window vs past query' distinction is operationally meaningless on real data.
ADOPTION_BARRIER: [Semantic query cache (GPTCache/Zilliz, GPT Semantic Cache arXiv:2411.05276) is a deployed standard achieving equal Pareto efficiency at matched skip-rate; A-RAG Context Tracker (arXiv:2602.03442) already implements live-window residency gating to prevent redundant retrieval; cheap signal is near-chance on real data (AUC 0.570 embedding, 0.554 lexical vs oracle 1.0, gap ~0.43) with embedding beating lexical by only +0.016; skipping costs ~2.6 F1 points vs always-retrieve (0.4765 vs 0.4505) and wrong skips are only partially recoverable (wrong-skip F1 0.17 vs correct-skip 0.52)]
RATIONALE: EXP-0018 L1 (CoQA 4,764 turns, MiniLM embedding, Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct via vLLM, 5,604 gens): M1=0.532 redundancy confirmed; gate vs cache @ matched skip F1 delta +0.0004 CI [-0.0045,+0.0053]; precision Δ CI straddles 0 for skip≥20% (e.g., 0.30: +0.013 [-0.005,+0.031]); AUC gate 0.570 vs lexical 0.554; A-RAG "Context Tracker" records read chunks to prevent redundant retrieval (arXiv:2602.03442 §3); GPTCache is practitioner standard (zilliz.com, HF forum 172433). Pre-registered kill-branches N1 (cache-matches) and N4 (prior-art) fire.
```
